1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:00,989
What if,

2
00:00:00,989 --> 00:00:02,972
in the worst week of a financial

3
00:00:02,972 --> 00:00:03,611
crisis,

4
00:00:03,611 --> 00:00:06,476
a carmaker in trouble suddenly became the

5
00:00:06,476 --> 00:00:09,280
most valuable company in the world?

6
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:10,870
Not for a year.

7
00:00:10,940 --> 00:00:12,370
Not for a month.

8
00:00:12,580 --> 00:00:14,154
For about a day.

9
00:00:19,417 --> 00:00:22,147
That happened to Volkswagen in October

10
00:00:22,147 --> 00:00:23,657
twenty oh eight.

11
00:00:23,887 --> 00:00:25,174
In two trading days,

12
00:00:25,174 --> 00:00:27,138
its share price jumped from about two

13
00:00:27,138 --> 00:00:29,755
hundred and sixty-six dollars to about one

14
00:00:29,755 --> 00:00:32,537
thousand two hundred and fifty dollars.

15
00:00:32,687 --> 00:00:34,020
For a brief moment,

16
00:00:34,020 --> 00:00:36,506
the whole company was worth about three

17
00:00:36,506 --> 00:00:38,968
hundred and seventy billion dollars,

18
00:00:38,968 --> 00:00:40,527
more than ExxonMobil,

19
00:00:40,527 --> 00:00:43,387
the world's biggest company at the time.

20
00:00:43,647 --> 00:00:46,197
Nothing about its cars had changed.

21
00:00:46,237 --> 00:00:48,301
What changed was a simple question of

22
00:00:48,301 --> 00:00:49,727
arithmetic.

23
00:00:49,987 --> 00:00:52,156
How many shares were left?

24
00:00:57,817 --> 00:01:01,296
Why would so many professional investors

25
00:01:01,296 --> 00:01:04,506
bet that Volkswagen's shares would fall?

26
00:01:06,817 --> 00:01:09,193
Let me draw how you bet against

27
00:01:09,193 --> 00:01:10,317
a share.

28
00:01:10,317 --> 00:01:12,317
It is called short selling.

29
00:01:12,317 --> 00:01:12,735
First,

30
00:01:12,735 --> 00:01:14,717
you borrow a share from someone who

31
00:01:14,717 --> 00:01:15,737
owns it.

32
00:01:15,737 --> 00:01:17,523
Then you sell it right away,

33
00:01:17,523 --> 00:01:19,027
at today's price.

34
00:01:19,227 --> 00:01:19,773
Later,

35
00:01:19,773 --> 00:01:21,093
you buy a share back on the

36
00:01:21,093 --> 00:01:23,577
market and return it to the lender.

37
00:01:23,617 --> 00:01:25,061
If the price has fallen,

38
00:01:25,061 --> 00:01:26,737
you keep the difference.

39
00:01:26,737 --> 00:01:28,233
But here is the catch:

40
00:01:28,233 --> 00:01:30,138
if the price rises instead,

41
00:01:30,138 --> 00:01:32,427
you still have to buy it back.

42
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:34,646
And a price can rise without any

43
00:01:34,646 --> 00:01:35,730
limit.

44
00:01:35,983 --> 00:01:37,470
In twenty oh eight,

45
00:01:37,470 --> 00:01:40,843
Volkswagen looked like an easy target.

46
00:01:40,973 --> 00:01:43,131
It was a carmaker carrying a lot

47
00:01:43,131 --> 00:01:44,163
of debt.

48
00:01:44,333 --> 00:01:46,391
Many hedge funds thought its shares had

49
00:01:46,391 --> 00:01:48,363
become too expensive.

50
00:01:48,483 --> 00:01:51,133
And then the financial crisis hit,

51
00:01:51,133 --> 00:01:54,143
and demand for new cars collapsed.

52
00:01:54,453 --> 00:01:56,377
If you wanted to bet that a

53
00:01:56,377 --> 00:01:57,314
share would fall,

54
00:01:57,314 --> 00:02:00,078
Volkswagen seemed like a good one.

55
00:02:00,317 --> 00:02:02,478
But there was one buyer who kept

56
00:02:02,478 --> 00:02:03,267
buying.

57
00:02:03,267 --> 00:02:03,748
Porsche,

58
00:02:03,748 --> 00:02:06,000
the sports car maker from Stuttgart,

59
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,000
much smaller than Volkswagen,

60
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,025
had been building up a stake in

61
00:02:10,025 --> 00:02:11,637
its giant neighbour.

62
00:02:12,037 --> 00:02:13,760
By March twenty oh eight,

63
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:15,758
Porsche owned thirty-one percent of

64
00:02:15,758 --> 00:02:17,107
Volkswagen.

65
00:02:17,257 --> 00:02:18,625
Would it go all the way to

66
00:02:18,625 --> 00:02:20,397
seventy-five percent?

67
00:02:20,517 --> 00:02:23,177
Porsche said that was very unlikely.

68
00:02:23,347 --> 00:02:25,157
The state of Lower Saxony,

69
00:02:25,157 --> 00:02:27,577
Volkswagen's second largest shareholder,

70
00:02:27,577 --> 00:02:29,397
owned twenty percent.

71
00:02:29,617 --> 00:02:31,899
So there simply weren't enough shares out

72
00:02:31,899 --> 00:02:32,707
there.

73
00:02:32,950 --> 00:02:35,390
So the bet looked safe.

74
00:02:35,390 --> 00:02:36,743
A weak carmaker,

75
00:02:36,743 --> 00:02:37,637
a crisis,

76
00:02:37,637 --> 00:02:40,300
and plenty of shares to borrow.

77
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:42,741
Or so everyone thought.

78
00:02:48,383 --> 00:02:51,459
What did the short sellers not know?

79
00:02:57,383 --> 00:02:58,332
On Sunday,

80
00:02:58,332 --> 00:03:00,012
October twenty-sixth,

81
00:03:00,012 --> 00:03:01,205
twenty oh eight,

82
00:03:01,205 --> 00:03:03,753
Porsche published a press release.

83
00:03:03,843 --> 00:03:05,884
It said that it held forty-two point

84
00:03:05,884 --> 00:03:08,379
six percent of Volkswagen's ordinary

85
00:03:08,379 --> 00:03:09,433
shares.

86
00:03:09,523 --> 00:03:11,092
And on top of that,

87
00:03:11,092 --> 00:03:13,220
thirty-one point five percent more in

88
00:03:13,220 --> 00:03:15,587
so-called cash-settled options,

89
00:03:15,587 --> 00:03:18,513
a kind of financial contract linked to

90
00:03:18,513 --> 00:03:20,443
Volkswagen's share price.

91
00:03:20,633 --> 00:03:21,475
Together,

92
00:03:21,475 --> 00:03:23,803
seventy-four point one percent.

93
00:03:23,943 --> 00:03:24,606
Its aim,

94
00:03:24,606 --> 00:03:25,270
it said,

95
00:03:25,270 --> 00:03:27,558
was to reach seventy-five percent in

96
00:03:27,558 --> 00:03:29,073
twenty oh nine.

97
00:03:29,273 --> 00:03:31,496
And the Porsche and Piëch families,

98
00:03:31,496 --> 00:03:34,218
who own all of Porsche's voting shares,

99
00:03:34,218 --> 00:03:36,465
backed the plan to take control of

100
00:03:36,465 --> 00:03:37,814
Volkswagen.

101
00:03:38,050 --> 00:03:40,170
Here is how they worked.

102
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:42,515
When an option was settled,

103
00:03:42,515 --> 00:03:44,284
Porsche would receive in cash the

104
00:03:44,284 --> 00:03:46,557
difference between Volkswagen's share

105
00:03:46,557 --> 00:03:48,300
price and an agreed price,

106
00:03:48,300 --> 00:03:49,910
called the strike.

107
00:03:50,160 --> 00:03:52,540
Those options were the surprise.

108
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:54,551
Porsche said they were there to protect

109
00:03:54,551 --> 00:03:56,770
it against rising prices.

110
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:58,776
Only a few weeks earlier,

111
00:03:58,776 --> 00:04:00,872
it had disclosed a stake of about

112
00:04:00,872 --> 00:04:02,520
thirty-five percent.

113
00:04:02,710 --> 00:04:04,484
Now the market could see the full

114
00:04:04,484 --> 00:04:05,127
picture,

115
00:04:05,127 --> 00:04:07,565
and it looked very different from what

116
00:04:07,565 --> 00:04:10,161
many short sellers had believed.

117
00:04:10,417 --> 00:04:12,397
Let me draw the problem with a

118
00:04:12,397 --> 00:04:13,987
hundred shares.

119
00:04:14,007 --> 00:04:14,514
Porsche:

120
00:04:14,514 --> 00:04:16,105
about seventy-four,

121
00:04:16,105 --> 00:04:17,857
counting its options.

122
00:04:17,917 --> 00:04:19,180
Lower Saxony:

123
00:04:19,180 --> 00:04:20,187
twenty.

124
00:04:20,477 --> 00:04:22,467
What is left for everyone else?

125
00:04:22,467 --> 00:04:24,127
Less than six.

126
00:04:24,177 --> 00:04:24,635
Now,

127
00:04:24,635 --> 00:04:27,187
how many shares had been sold short?

128
00:04:27,187 --> 00:04:28,627
Around twelve.

129
00:04:28,627 --> 00:04:29,960
Twelve shares owed,

130
00:04:29,960 --> 00:04:32,367
and fewer than six for sale.

131
00:04:32,387 --> 00:04:35,637
Not every short seller could buy back.

132
00:04:35,637 --> 00:04:37,550
That is a short squeeze.

133
00:04:37,783 --> 00:04:39,054
On Monday morning,

134
00:04:39,054 --> 00:04:41,163
the trading floors opened.

135
00:04:41,183 --> 00:04:44,068
And everyone who owed shares went looking

136
00:04:44,068 --> 00:04:45,630
for the same few.

137
00:04:51,283 --> 00:04:54,638
What happens when everyone has to buy,

138
00:04:54,638 --> 00:04:57,393
and almost no one can sell?

139
00:05:00,283 --> 00:05:02,603
The price explodes.

140
00:05:02,603 --> 00:05:03,493
On Friday,

141
00:05:03,493 --> 00:05:05,777
a Volkswagen share had cost about two

142
00:05:05,777 --> 00:05:08,203
hundred and sixty-six dollars.

143
00:05:08,343 --> 00:05:09,227
By Tuesday,

144
00:05:09,227 --> 00:05:10,565
October twenty-eighth,

145
00:05:10,565 --> 00:05:13,059
it touched about one thousand two hundred

146
00:05:13,059 --> 00:05:14,793
and fifty dollars.

147
00:05:14,873 --> 00:05:16,529
Short sellers were not buying because they

148
00:05:16,529 --> 00:05:18,203
liked the company.

149
00:05:18,203 --> 00:05:20,953
They were buying because they had to.

150
00:05:21,083 --> 00:05:23,621
Every purchase pushed the price higher,

151
00:05:23,621 --> 00:05:25,328
which made the losses of the next

152
00:05:25,328 --> 00:05:27,421
short seller even bigger.

153
00:05:27,683 --> 00:05:29,525
And for a brief moment,

154
00:05:29,525 --> 00:05:31,993
the numbers became absurd.

155
00:05:32,343 --> 00:05:33,224
At that price,

156
00:05:33,224 --> 00:05:35,257
Volkswagen's voting shares were worth

157
00:05:35,257 --> 00:05:37,741
about three hundred and seventy billion

158
00:05:37,741 --> 00:05:38,773
dollars.

159
00:05:38,773 --> 00:05:39,999
ExxonMobil,

160
00:05:39,999 --> 00:05:42,252
the giant oil company and the world's

161
00:05:42,252 --> 00:05:43,729
most valuable firm,

162
00:05:43,729 --> 00:05:45,982
was worth three hundred and forty-three

163
00:05:45,982 --> 00:05:47,583
billion dollars.

164
00:05:47,883 --> 00:05:50,379
A carmaker in the middle of a

165
00:05:50,379 --> 00:05:51,352
crisis was,

166
00:05:51,352 --> 00:05:52,325
on paper,

167
00:05:52,325 --> 00:05:55,920
the most valuable company on the planet.

168
00:05:56,183 --> 00:05:58,046
On the trading floors,

169
00:05:58,046 --> 00:05:59,573
it was chaos.

170
00:05:59,573 --> 00:06:01,735
One analyst in London said he had

171
00:06:01,735 --> 00:06:04,330
hedge fund managers literally in tears on

172
00:06:04,330 --> 00:06:05,363
the phone.

173
00:06:05,603 --> 00:06:08,023
And Germany's financial regulator,

174
00:06:08,023 --> 00:06:08,613
BaFin,

175
00:06:08,613 --> 00:06:10,036
said the same day that it was

176
00:06:10,036 --> 00:06:12,680
examining the trading for signs of insider

177
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:15,313
trading or market manipulation.

178
00:06:15,683 --> 00:06:18,458
Porsche denied all of it.

179
00:06:18,717 --> 00:06:21,937
A price like that could not last.

180
00:06:21,937 --> 00:06:24,073
But who would let the air out?

181
00:06:29,717 --> 00:06:31,654
How do you stop a squeeze once

182
00:06:31,654 --> 00:06:33,361
it has started?

183
00:06:38,717 --> 00:06:42,187
The first move came from Porsche itself.

184
00:06:42,377 --> 00:06:44,020
On October twenty-ninth,

185
00:06:44,020 --> 00:06:45,477
it said that short sellers were

186
00:06:45,477 --> 00:06:48,157
responsible for the extreme prices.

187
00:06:48,347 --> 00:06:50,539
To avoid more market distortions,

188
00:06:50,539 --> 00:06:52,975
it would settle options covering up to

189
00:06:52,975 --> 00:06:55,167
five percent of Volkswagen's shares,

190
00:06:55,167 --> 00:06:57,381
putting more shares within reach of those

191
00:06:57,381 --> 00:06:58,867
who needed them.

192
00:06:59,197 --> 00:07:01,351
Porsche added that it had informed the

193
00:07:01,351 --> 00:07:03,459
regulator in advance.

194
00:07:03,717 --> 00:07:05,933
The second move came from the stock

195
00:07:05,933 --> 00:07:06,947
exchange.

196
00:07:06,947 --> 00:07:08,567
Deutsche Börse runs the DAX,

197
00:07:08,567 --> 00:07:12,187
the index of Germany's top companies.

198
00:07:12,257 --> 00:07:13,416
After Tuesday's close,

199
00:07:13,416 --> 00:07:15,576
Volkswagen alone made up twenty-seven

200
00:07:15,576 --> 00:07:17,437
percent of the whole index.

201
00:07:17,437 --> 00:07:20,986
So the exchange brought forward a rule,

202
00:07:20,986 --> 00:07:23,916
and capped Volkswagen's weight at ten

203
00:07:23,916 --> 00:07:25,167
percent.

204
00:07:25,247 --> 00:07:25,965
Normally,

205
00:07:25,965 --> 00:07:27,991
that rule was only applied on fixed

206
00:07:27,991 --> 00:07:28,525
dates,

207
00:07:28,525 --> 00:07:29,998
and the next one was not until

208
00:07:29,998 --> 00:07:31,807
December twenty-second.

209
00:07:31,807 --> 00:07:32,534
This time,

210
00:07:32,534 --> 00:07:34,515
it would apply from Monday,

211
00:07:34,515 --> 00:07:36,118
November third.

212
00:07:36,383 --> 00:07:38,883
Let me draw why that mattered.

213
00:07:38,913 --> 00:07:40,661
An index is like a basket of

214
00:07:40,661 --> 00:07:41,833
companies.

215
00:07:41,833 --> 00:07:44,221
Many funds simply copy the basket,

216
00:07:44,221 --> 00:07:46,793
holding each company at its weight.

217
00:07:46,873 --> 00:07:49,487
When one company becomes a giant slice

218
00:07:49,487 --> 00:07:50,652
of the basket,

219
00:07:50,652 --> 00:07:52,292
those funds need more of it,

220
00:07:52,292 --> 00:07:54,423
at the worst possible moment.

221
00:07:54,423 --> 00:07:56,545
Cap the slice at ten percent,

222
00:07:56,545 --> 00:07:58,757
and that pressure eases.

223
00:07:59,017 --> 00:08:01,378
And the price came down as fast

224
00:08:01,378 --> 00:08:03,327
as it went up.

225
00:08:03,537 --> 00:08:04,735
On Wednesday,

226
00:08:04,735 --> 00:08:07,180
the share closed at about six hundred

227
00:08:07,180 --> 00:08:08,622
and sixty dollars,

228
00:08:08,622 --> 00:08:10,578
about half its peak of the day

229
00:08:10,578 --> 00:08:11,667
before.

230
00:08:11,917 --> 00:08:13,790
Within four days of the peak,

231
00:08:13,790 --> 00:08:16,287
it had fallen fifty-eight percent.

232
00:08:16,377 --> 00:08:17,475
A month later,

233
00:08:17,475 --> 00:08:19,867
it was down seventy percent.

234
00:08:20,127 --> 00:08:22,032
But for many short sellers,

235
00:08:22,032 --> 00:08:23,597
it was too late.

236
00:08:23,697 --> 00:08:26,014
They had already bought back at sky-high

237
00:08:26,014 --> 00:08:27,077
prices.

238
00:08:27,237 --> 00:08:29,058
Hedge funds that had bet against

239
00:08:29,058 --> 00:08:31,920
Volkswagen lost an estimated thirty

240
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:33,561
billion dollars.

241
00:08:33,817 --> 00:08:35,932
Porsche seemed to be winning one of

242
00:08:35,932 --> 00:08:38,752
the most spectacular takeover battles in

243
00:08:38,752 --> 00:08:40,527
German history.

244
00:08:40,817 --> 00:08:43,980
The real ending was very different.

245
00:08:49,617 --> 00:08:52,799
So who really won?

246
00:08:58,617 --> 00:08:59,897
On paper,

247
00:08:59,897 --> 00:09:02,137
Porsche looked brilliant.

248
00:09:02,237 --> 00:09:04,605
For its business year twenty oh seven

249
00:09:04,605 --> 00:09:05,875
to twenty oh eight,

250
00:09:05,875 --> 00:09:08,028
it reported a gain of about ten

251
00:09:08,028 --> 00:09:10,396
billion dollars on its Volkswagen options

252
00:09:10,396 --> 00:09:11,427
alone.

253
00:09:11,677 --> 00:09:12,735
A year earlier,

254
00:09:12,735 --> 00:09:14,895
it had already made about four point

255
00:09:14,895 --> 00:09:17,007
nine billion dollars this way.

256
00:09:17,477 --> 00:09:19,384
That was most of its profit of

257
00:09:19,384 --> 00:09:22,367
about twelve point seven billion dollars.

258
00:09:22,647 --> 00:09:24,341
A large part of a sports car

259
00:09:24,341 --> 00:09:26,519
maker's profit came from financial

260
00:09:26,519 --> 00:09:29,780
contracts on another company's shares.

261
00:09:30,017 --> 00:09:32,027
But the plan was to take over

262
00:09:32,027 --> 00:09:33,006
Volkswagen,

263
00:09:33,006 --> 00:09:35,867
and the crisis made that much harder.

264
00:09:36,047 --> 00:09:37,452
Less than a year later,

265
00:09:37,452 --> 00:09:39,367
the roles were reversed.

266
00:09:39,367 --> 00:09:41,125
In August twenty oh nine,

267
00:09:41,125 --> 00:09:43,727
the two companies agreed to merge.

268
00:09:43,767 --> 00:09:46,111
Volkswagen would first buy forty-two

269
00:09:46,111 --> 00:09:48,455
percent of Porsche for four point seven

270
00:09:48,455 --> 00:09:49,731
billion dollars,

271
00:09:49,731 --> 00:09:52,075
and Porsche would become a brand inside

272
00:09:52,075 --> 00:09:53,977
the Volkswagen group.

273
00:09:54,157 --> 00:09:55,916
Volkswagen's chief executive,

274
00:09:55,916 --> 00:09:57,081
Martin Winterkorn,

275
00:09:57,081 --> 00:09:58,867
would run both companies.

276
00:09:58,887 --> 00:10:00,761
And the Gulf state of Qatar was

277
00:10:00,761 --> 00:10:03,104
expected to take a direct stake in

278
00:10:03,104 --> 00:10:04,017
Volkswagen,

279
00:10:04,017 --> 00:10:06,257
by buying options that Porsche held.

280
00:10:06,437 --> 00:10:08,641
The news agency AFP called it the

281
00:10:08,641 --> 00:10:10,844
failure of a gamble to take over

282
00:10:10,844 --> 00:10:12,927
the far larger Volkswagen.

283
00:10:12,927 --> 00:10:15,817
The hunter had become the hunted.

284
00:10:16,083 --> 00:10:17,523
And the courts?

285
00:10:17,663 --> 00:10:20,213
Prosecutors in Stuttgart charged Porsche's

286
00:10:20,213 --> 00:10:22,044
former chief executive,

287
00:10:22,044 --> 00:10:23,643
Wendelin Wiedeking,

288
00:10:23,643 --> 00:10:25,475
and its former finance chief,

289
00:10:25,475 --> 00:10:26,379
Holger Härter,

290
00:10:26,379 --> 00:10:28,833
with market manipulation.

291
00:10:29,153 --> 00:10:30,794
